# Reminder-only beat for demo step 3: the truncated log, no root type.
#
# This beat never drives protolens — it only paces the presenter and shows
# short reminders in the script pane. The presenter runs the overrides and
# heat cues by hand. Advance each step with space or Enter.
#
# Invocation (from grehack2026.sh):
#   protolens --descriptor-set life.desc eve/server.log \
#       --script beats/logfile

title: A blob with no schema

steps:
  - text: |
      server.log, opened against life.desc only.

      protolens opens it, but no known root type matches — instead of a
      type name you get a generic `message`. And the tail is flagged
      TRUNCATED: that is exactly why protoc --decode_raw choked.

      👋 Fold the message (`1`) so the top-level entries fit on screen.

  - text: |
      Enable the heat cues — press `i`.

      Every substructure gets a cue showing how well the corpus can type
      it. The brighter the cue, the more confident the match. protolens
      still recognizes the Request and Response shapes from their fields.

      👋 Press `i`, then hover over the bright cues.

  - text: |
      Pin the recognized types with an override (the override pane, or the
      prefilled command protolens proposes on a cue). Request and Response
      are shaped differently enough — a varint where the other has a
      length-delimited field — that the scoring does not confuse them.

      👋 Commit the proposed overrides for the Request / Response leaves.

  - text: |
      That is the realistic case: a truncated blob, no matching root type,
      and we still reconstruct the record — type by type — from the field
      shapes the corpus does know.

      👋 Type `:q` to quit protolens.
